<title>UK: IBCA assigns l-term A plus to HSBC CDs.</title>
<headline>IBCA assigns l-term A plus to HSBC CDs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBCA, the European credit rating agency, said on Wednesday it has assigned a long-term rating of A plus to the HK$2.0 billion floating rate certificates of deposit due 2002 issued by HongKong and Sanghai Banking Corporation (HSBC).  </p>
<p>HongkongBank is the largest bank in Hong Kong and has operations in 29 countries, IBCA said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- International Bonds Unit +44 171 542 8682</p>
